the mandalorian is back with a vengeance  and there's a lot for fans of classic  star wars to sink their teeth into  from the appearance of the infamous  crate dragon to a certain fan favorite  character emerging at the very end of  the episode  there's a lot to unpack plus that's not  even getting into all of the fun easter  eggs associated with the story taking  place on tatooine  complete with jawas and tuscan raiders  in the first episode of season 2  mando ends up forming a truce of sorts  between the townspeople of mars pelgo  and the raiders in the desert and the  sand people are willing to help  they rain on mine  however while tuscan raiders have been  in the star wars universe since the very  beginning  there's still quite a lot casual fans  don't know about them for starters a lot  of people may be unaware of what a  tuscan raider even looks like  throughout the various star wars  properties tuscan raiders are adorned  with masks gloves and long ropes but  imagine all that clothing makes things  pretty hot considering they're on a  desert planet but the aliens have  probably become accustomed to it by this  point however that still doesn't answer  the question of what a tuscan raider  would look like naked  if that's something you're wondering  about well wonder no more  there have been a few places over the  years where you could have seen what  tuscan raiders look like with their  masks off  maybe believe it or not you can get a  pretty good picture of what a tuscan  raider actually looks like under their  hood  by simply looking to the past over the  years the aliens have made a handful of  massless appearances throughout the star  wars universe the first time a tuscan  was ever seen by fans without a mask was  in the 1997 video game  jedi knight dark forces too there's a  group in the game known as grave tuscans  who appear to have cat-like features  however since it's an old video game  it's hard to get a clear idea of what a  tuscan looks like under the mask without  squinting  some clarity came a few years later when  a half-mast tuscan raider appeared in  star wars republic issue 62.  in this comic book anakin has a  nightmarish vision which includes a  tuscan showing off the left side of its  face  since it's a dream sequence the image is  somewhat distorted  so it's still a little difficult to make  out key characters of this race  that said this depiction isn't  necessarily accurate because it is  entirely possible anakin had no idea  what a tuscan raider looked like  in other words this image could have  been his psyche filling in the blanks  and installing a monstrous creature  there  which would make sense considering they  kidnapped his mother  in other words these images may not be  all that accurate when it comes to  understanding the tuscans  that said another piece of star wars  media may finally solve this mystery in  a different way  anyone who watched the season 1 finale  of the mandalorian knows that din jaren  wasn't born a mandalorian  he was adopted later in life suggesting  that being a mandalorian is more of  something you choose than something you  must be born into  it would certainly make sense  considering that mando's even referred  to his way of life as a religion in the  past  and based on one comic it appears as  though something similar may be going on  with tuscan raiders  in star wars republic issue 59 anakin  encounters asherad hett  who wears tuscan gob that is until he  takes off his mask  revealing himself to be human he goes  into a bit of his backstory  explaining how his mother came to live  with the tuscans a long time ago  later in the comic he reveals that  humans aren't genetically compatible  with tuscans and it is potentially  suggested that these raiders have a  bunch of different races living among  them  of course it's worth pointing out that  these comics are no longer part of the  official canon  so it's not necessarily proof of what  the raiders look like under their masks  still similarly to how we eventually saw  mando without his mask perhaps the show  will eventually show us a tuscan raider  unmasked in all of its glory  and end this mystery for good check out  one of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about your  favorite star wars characters are coming  soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one  [Music]
 

